$ opod connect curl
--- exit 0
--- stdout
# curl → Opod — useful for smoke tests

# OpenAI shape:
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:1/v1/chat/completions \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer transcript-admin-key" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "model": "auto",
    "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "hi in 5 words"}]
  }'

# Anthropic shape (same endpoint, different path + headers):
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:1/v1/messages \
  -H "x-api-key: transcript-admin-key" \
  -H "anthropic-version: 2023-06-01" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "model": "auto",
    "max_tokens": 64,
    "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "hi in 5 words"}]
  }'
--- stderr
⚠ this snippet carries this leader's admin key, which can manage the whole leader — give curl its own key instead: opod token create curl, then --token <that key>
